# API Configuration Template
# ================================================
# This file should be used as a template for local configuration.
# DO NOT commit this file with actual API keys!
# 
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Edit .env with your actual API keys
# 3. The .env file is in .gitignore and will NOT be committed
# 4. Load these values in your code using System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable()

# ================================================
# OPENAI API CONFIGURATION
# ================================================
# Get your key from: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# Format: sk-proj-...
# Required: Yes (for GPT-4o model)
# Cost: ~$0.03-0.06 per 1K tokens (depends on model version)
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ================================================
# GOOGLE GEMINI API CONFIGURATION
# ================================================
# Get your key from: https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey
# Format: Long alphanumeric string
# Required: No (optional, for Gemini 2.5 Pro model)
# Cost: Free tier available (15 requests/min)
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ================================================
# DEEPSEEK API CONFIGURATION
# ================================================
# Get your key from: https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
# Format: sk-...
# Required: No (optional, for DeepSeek VL model)
# Cost: Check https://platform.deepseek.com/pricing
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# ================================================
# POSTHOG ANALYTICS CONFIGURATION (OPTIONAL)
# ================================================
# Get your key from: https://app.posthog.com/project/settings
# Required: No (analytics only, can be left empty)
# Warning: PostHog sends prompt and response text - only enable if using non-sensitive data
POSTHOG_API_KEY=
POSTHOG_HOST=https://app.posthog.com

# ================================================
# OLLAMA LOCAL CONFIGURATION
# ================================================
# Ollama runs locally - no API key needed
# Download from: https://ollama.ai/download
# Model: llava (recommended for vision+language)
# Cost: Free (runs on your machine)
OLLAMA_API_URL=http://localhost:11434/api/generate
OLLAMA_MODEL=llava

# ================================================
# DEVELOPMENT SETTINGS
# ================================================
# Set to true to enable debug logging
DEBUG_ENABLED=false

# ================================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ================================================
# 1. OpenAI GPT-4o (Recommended):
#    - Go to https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#    - Click "Create new secret key"
#    - Paste the key below (format: sk-proj-...)
#
# 2. Google Gemini 2.5 Pro:
#    - Go to https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey
#    - Click "Create API key"
#    - Copy the generated key
#
# 3. DeepSeek VL (Optional):
#    - Go to https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
#    - Create an API key
#    - Add billing if needed
#
# 4. Ollama (Local, Free):
#    - Download from https://ollama.ai/download
#    - Run: ollama serve
#    - In another terminal: ollama pull llava
#    - No API key needed!
#
# 5. PostHog (Optional Analytics):
#    - Create account at https://posthog.com/
#    - Leave empty to disable analytics
#    - Only enable if using non-sensitive test data

# ================================================
# IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTES
# ================================================
# - This .env file is in .gitignore and will NOT be committed
# - Never commit actual API keys to the repository
# - If you accidentally expose a key:
#   1. Revoke it immediately in the service dashboard
#   2. Generate a new key
#   3. Update this .env file
#   4. If committed, contact repository maintainers
#
# - Load these in C# code:
#   string openaiKey = System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("OPENAI_API_KEY");
#
# - Test your setup:
#   Run APIConfigurationTest script in Unity to verify all connections

# ================================================
# COST MANAGEMENT
# ================================================
# OpenAI:
#   - Monitor at: https://platform.openai.com/account/billing/overview
#   - Set limits at: https://platform.openai.com/account/billing/limits
#   - Recommended: Set $5-10/month limit during development
#
# Gemini:
#   - Free tier: 15 requests/minute
#   - Paid tier: More capacity, check Google Cloud pricing
#
# DeepSeek:
#   - Check https://platform.deepseek.com/pricing
#   - Set monthly spending limits if available

# ================================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ================================================
# "API key not set":
#   - Verify this file exists (.env)
#   - Check you're loading from environment variable correctly
#   - Restart your IDE/terminal after creating .env
#
# "401 Unauthorized":
#   - API key is invalid or expired
#   - Regenerate it in the service dashboard
#
# "Connection refused" (for Ollama):
#   - Make sure Ollama server is running
#   - Run: ollama serve
#   - Check port 11434 is available
#
# "Rate limited":
#   - Reduce request frequency
#   - Upgrade to paid tier
#   - Use local Ollama instead of cloud APIs

# ================================================
# QUICK SETUP CHECKLIST
# ================================================
# [ ] Copy this file: cp .env.example .env
# [ ] Add OPENAI_API_KEY (or alternative model key)
# [ ] Add GEMINI_API_KEY (optional)
# [ ] Add DEEPSEEK_API_KEY (optional)
# [ ] For local-only setup: Install Ollama and skip cloud APIs
# [ ] Verify .env is in .gitignore
# [ ] Test configuration in Unity (APIConfigurationTest)
# [ ] Never commit .env file!

